      "claim": "Engraulis species (e.g., E. encrasicolus, E. ringens) have an optimal temperature range for growth and reproduction of roughly 12 °C to 24 °C.",
      "evidence": "Laboratory growth experiments and field spawning data reported in FAO species fact sheets and peer‑reviewed studies (e.g., Rivas et al., 2015; Santos et al., 2018) show peak growth rates and highest recruitment within this window.",
