      "claim": "The majority of global anchovy biomass is concentrated in coastal upwelling systems where surface temperatures are typically 12 °C–18 °C.",
      "evidence": "FAO fishery statistics (2022) indicate that the Peruvian/Humboldt, Benguela, and California upwelling zones together account for >80 % of reported anchovy catches; satellite SST records for these regions show mean surface temperatures in the 12‑18 °C range.",
