      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Consequently, more anchovies live in warmer (or at least not‑cold) waters than in colder waters.",
      "evidence": "Combining steps 1‑4: the bulk of biomass resides in 12‑18 °C upwelling zones (Step 2), which are above the cold threshold defined in Step 3, while Step 4 shows virtually no anchovies in waters <12 °C. Hence the total number in non‑cold waters exceeds that in cold waters.",
